<title>SINGAPORE: India tenders to sell August 9-11 Bombay LAN.</title>
<headline>India tenders to sell August 9-11 Bombay LAN.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) is to issue a tender to sell 25,000-tonnes of low aromatic naphtha (LAN) lifting August 9-11 from Bombay on the west coast, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender closes July 31 and is valid for a day.</p>
<p>IOC's last LAN cargo from Bombay, lifting July 20-22,  was awarded to Swiss trader Glencore at $33.75 per tonne discount to spot U.S. Gulf 87 octane gasoline quotes on a free-on-board basis.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3086)</p>
